  "worked_solution": "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & 2 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 10+2\\cdot 3\\, & \\,\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 15+2\\cdot 6 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 10+\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 3\\, & \\,(-1)\\cdot 15+\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6+6\\, & \\,9+12 \\\\ -10+4\\, & \\,-15+8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 21 \\\\ -6 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
